 "kind": "recipe",
 "metadata": {
  "alignment": "unspecified",
  "description": "Single-DGX-Spark NVIDIA Nemotron 3.5 Lightning 30B-A3B (Mamba-2, attention and MoE hybrid) on Ash Hart's TensorFold engine v0.4.0 (exact decoding, custom CUDA kernels JIT-compiled on first start, stock upstream source) with Vontra's MLX 4-bit (group 64) checkpoint, which includes the model's MTP draft head. One rank only: TensorFold's two-rank mode is not available here. Requests are served one at a time (upstream CUDA behaviour for Nemotron) in TensorFold's default 16,384-token window; raise the context setting for longer prompts, up to the model's 262,144 tokens, subject to TensorFold's startup memory check. Upstream measured about 123 to 146 tok/s with MTP and a 42.2 GiB peak at 262,144 tokens on a 64 GB M5 Pro, an MLX run with TensorFold 0.3.5.1; no DGX Spark figure is published, and none is measured here. Licence, for information: NVIDIA Nemotron 3.5 Lightning weights are under the OpenMDW License Agreement 1.1 (text in the model repository); TensorFold is MIT.",
  "tags": [
   "engine",
   "kernel-jit",
   "mamba",
   "mlx-checkpoint",
   "moe",
   "mtp",
   "nemotron",
   "reasoning",
   "spark",
   "tensorfold"
  ],
  "title": "Nemotron 3.5 Lightning 30B A3B TensorFold single Spark"
 },
